ged  and if they are if they're able to  afford to  pay for private education they must be  able to afford technology and  private tutors but most of the country  can't  merza lives with his mom and five  brothers and sisters  he's hoping to have a career in finance  but he's worried that cancelling exams  will put him at a disadvantage  i mean i can't imagine any student who  doesn't share  that sort of anxious feeling because you  when when you do exams right you sort of  take things into your own hands  and you sort of just you know use your  own ability to get the results you want  however  this time around it's the teachers who  sort of have the  power in their hands and they sort of  decide your future um  looking back at all the exams you've  done and how you performed in class  um just knowing that sort of knowledge  you know  someone else is sort of governing your  decision whether that's going to  university or whatever  you want to do in the future is it's  quite um  yeah it definitely gives the anxious  feeling in a survey of young people who  work with the social mobility foundation  shared exclusively with safety ridge on  sunday  73 of students said they're anxious  about exams being cancelled  64 said their mental health has been  negatively impacted by school closures  four in ten said they don't have access  to reliable broadband  and 38 said they haven't been contacted  by their school or college  about their technology needs boris  johnson said  that closing schools was a last resort  and it's not hard to understand  why for children who don't have the  right equipment  or frankly the right home environment to  learn in things are really tough  and the uncertainty too is clearly  taking its toll on young people's mental  health  social workers struggling under an  increased caseload are also concerned  i've been qualified as a social worker  since  2005 and i've been working with children  and family  for for nearly well for over 20 years  now  and i've never experienced a time in my  professional  life when services have been under so  much pressure  and so much strain people who have  lost their jobs have been furloughed  people that are on low incomes you know  spending time  at home with each other all of the time  with  really limited resources has seen  a real increase in the complexity  and the harm that some of our young  children have experienced  under the pressure of rising cases and  new variants closing schools was perhaps  inevitable what's important now is a  roadmap to reopening  and a plan to make sure disadvantaged  children aren't another victim  of the pandemic
 

